{"name":"Leprechaun Laugh","hex":"#8cc37d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"leprechaun","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of diminutive, solitary fairy or sprite, traditionally depicted as a small, bearded man wearing a green coat and hat, often found repairing a single shoe; they typically possess hidden treasure, such as a pot of gold hidden at the end of a rainbow, and can be forced to reveal its location if captured.","An Irish person."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leprechaun"},{"term":"laugh","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An expression of mirth particular to the human species; the sound heard in laughing; laughter.","Something that provokes mirth or scorn."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To show mirth, satisfaction, or derision, by peculiar movement of the muscles of the face, particularly of the mouth, causing a lighting up of the face and eyes, and usually accompanied by the emission of explosive or chuckling sounds from the chest and throat; to indulge in laughter.","To be or appear cheerful, pleasant, mirthful, lively, or brilliant; to sparkle; to sport."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/laugh"}],"entries":[{"title":"Leprechaun","blocks":[{"text":"A leprechaun is a diminutive supernatural being in Irish folklore, classed by some as a type of solitary fairy. They are usually depicted as little bearded men, wearing a coat and hat, who partake in mischief. In later times, they have been depicted as shoe-makers who have a hidden pot of gold at the end of the rainbow."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Leprechaun_ill_artlibre_jnl.png/330px-Leprechaun_ill_artlibre_jnl.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leprechaun"},{"title":"Laughter","blocks":[{"text":"Laughter is a typically pleasant physical reaction and emotion consisting usually of rhythmical, usually audible contractions of the diaphragm and other parts of the respiratory system. It is a response to certain external or internal stimuli. Laughter can rise from such stimuli as being tickled, or from humorous stories, imagery, videos or thoughts. Most commonly, it is considered an auditory expression of a number of positive emotional states, such as joy, mirth, happiness or relief. On some occasions, however, it may be caused by contrary emotional states such as embarrassment, surprise, or confusion such as nervous laughter or courtesy laugh. Age, gender, education, language and culture are all indicators as to whether a person will experience laughter in a given situation. Other than humans, some other species of primate express laughter-like vocalizations in response to physical contact such as wrestling, play chasing or tickling."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Laughing_boy_at_golden_hour.jpg/330px-Laughing_boy_at_golden_hour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laughter"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Leprechaun_engraving_1900.jpg/330px-Leprechaun_engraving_1900.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Leprechaun_engraving_1900.jpg/330px-Leprechaun_engraving_1900.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A leprechaun counts his gold in this engraving c. 1900","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALeprechaun_engraving_1900.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Menwithleprechaun.jpg/500px-Menwithleprechaun.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Menwithleprechaun.jpg/500px-Menwithleprechaun.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_ca